86066151 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069135 #edb/ref 1069 "q-215707" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069135 #edb/ref 1071 "Solve the absolute value inequality $\\mid \\frac{5 - 9a}{2} \\mid \\ge 7$.$a$\n{{field-1}} {{field-2}}\nor $a \\ge$\n{{field-3}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069135 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a92a4124-bc7c-5436-968f-ce759fb4d648" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069604 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186069605 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069604 #edb/ref 1061 145541 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069604 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "e46e2f60-2005-54d4-8f5c-97b81542dd48" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069604 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186070026 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069605 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186069606 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069605 #edb/ref 1061 145542 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069605 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "461b27d5-3e08-5e71-9e57-464e06a7b559" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069605 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186068717 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069606 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186069607 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069606 #edb/ref 1061 145546 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069606 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "95df2774-fa6c-5c44-85c3-1203c060ec1a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069606 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186068718 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069607 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186069608 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069607 #edb/ref 1061 145550 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069607 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "3706f0b6-4695-54b2-974b-2b4f77638739" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069607 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186070027 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069608 #edb/ref 1061 145551 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069608 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "419f8ba9-27c0-5918-8ecd-eff659df7bb5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069608 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186068719 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186070026 #edb/ref 1064 "**Absolute value inequalities** combine two basic concepts: absolute value and inequality. The absolute value of a number is its distance from zero, while an inequality specifies a range of values.\n\nConsider a simple absolute value inequality, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\mid x \\mid < 7\n$$\n\nThis inequality specifies every number $x$ that is less than a distance of $7$ from $0$. So, it represents the same thing as the following compound inequality:\n\n$$\n-7 < x < 7\n$$\n\nTo solve an absolute value inequality, we first convert it to a compound inequality to remove the absolute value. Then, we can solve the compound inequality using the usual methods.\n\nTo illustrate, let's solve the following inequality:\n\n$$\n\\mid 2x+3 \\mid \\leq 5\n$$\n\nFirst, we interpret the inequality: the inequality specifies every number $2x+3$ whose distance from zero is less than or equal to $5$. So, it represents the same thing as the following compound inequality:\n\n$$\n-5 \\leq 2x+3 \\leq 5\n$$\n\nNow, we can solve the compound inequality using the usual methods:\n\n$$\n-5 \\le 2x + 3 \\le 5; - 8 \\le 2x \\le 2; - 4 \\le x \\le 1\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186070026 #edb/ref 1065 8825 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186070026 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "53ecd5cc-486a-584d-abc8-f75ec26f12cc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186070026 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186070027 #edb/ref 1064 "We take a similar approach for absolute value inequalities involving the \"greater than\" symbol. To illustrate, consider the following absolute value inequality:\n\n$$\n\\mid x \\mid \\geq 6\n$$\n\nTo solve this absolute value inequality, we convert it into a compound inequality to remove the absolute value. The inequality specifies every number $x$ whose distance from zero is greater than or equal to $6$. This corresponds to the following compound inequality:\n\n$$\nx\\begin{vmatrix}\\le - 6 & or & x\\end{vmatrix}\\ge 6\n$$\n\nWe use the word \"or\" instead of \"and\" since only one of the inequalities\n\n$$\nx\\leq-6\n$$\n\nor\n\n$$\nx\\geq 6\n$$\n\nneeds to be true for\n\n$$\n\\mid x \\mid \\geq 6\n$$\n\nto be true." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186070027 #edb/ref 1065 8830 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186070027 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "93e8452a-53ea-5e58-807a-00e95af99af1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186070027 #edb/ref 1067 "Greater Than (or Equal To) Absolute Value Inequalities" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
